**Definition 9.1 (which labels are counted).** Count actual acquired
outcomes whose jointly counted whole fibre has dimension at most two
and whose supported decoded live CP map is nonzero. Ignore null and
supported-live-zero outcomes. The count is neither a total alphabet,
a real-atom count, a grouped rank nor an inaccessible representation
multiplicity. In the stipulated integral class a finite count means
that the accessible live-bearing subinstrument is concentrated on that
many actual record values of nonzero integrated CP mass, modulo null
outcomes. A positive nonatomic accessible live-bearing component has
infinitely many labels. An unacquired integral index is encoder Kraus
multiplicity of a coarse actual label, with ONE common decoder.

